hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1517","Ahmad bin Abdah told us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, told us, Abu Hazim, on the authority of Sahl bin Saad, he said: There was a fight between the Banu Amr ibn Awf. This was reported to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, so he prayed the noon prayer, then he came to them to reconcile between them, then he said to Bilal: “O Bilal, “If the afternoon prayer has come and I have not arrived, then command Abu Bakr and let him lead the people in prayer,” and he mentioned the hadith in its length. It was mentioned in the report: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came, stood behind Abu Bakr, and motioned to him: “Continue with your prayer.”"
